v 3
d connectedness. VAR-type, TVP-VAR and DCC-GARCH connectedness measures
d
d Estimates the connectedness measures of Diebold and Yilmaz (2009, 2012) from static
d and rolling-window VARs, quantile and LAD VARs, (adaptive) LASSO, ridge and
d elastic-net VARs and the TVP-VAR connectedness measures of Antonakakis,
d Chatziantoniou and Gabauer (2020), with corrected total, pairwise and influence
d indices, row or scalar normalization, clustered identification (Buchwalter, Diebold
d and Yilmaz 2026), frequency connectedness (Barunik and Krehlik 2018), joint and
d extended joint connectedness, R2 decomposed and model-free connectedness, DCC-GARCH
d volatility connectedness (Gabauer 2020) and its R2 decomposition, asymmetric
d (positive and negative) connectedness and the spillover asymmetry measure, group
d measures (aggregated, conditional, inclusive, exclusive, internal, external),
d bootstrap inference (also for the spillover asymmetry measure) and event tests,
d network plots, and portfolio and hedging strategies (minimum connectedness,
d multivariate hedging, risk-parity, bivariate portfolios, hedge ratios). Port of
d the ConnectednessApproach R package by David Gabauer (GPL-3).
d Includes 19 datasets from published applications.
d
d Requires: Stata 16.1 or newer
d Author: Nikolaos Antonakakis, University of Nicosia
d Support: antonakakis.n@unic.ac.cy
d Distribution-Date: 20261025
d License: GPL-3
